data phantom_marker_emitted_beside_a_same_named_type_definition: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "phantom_marker_emitted_beside_a_same_named_type_definition" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "an executing emit-and-build control over a coproduct whose arms name a local record, an imported record and a unit variant, enrolled where it runs on every change to the Rust emitter, so a marker beside a declaration it shadows is refused before a consumer crate reaches rustc; and a type declaration index covering every type item kind, so no local item can resolve as NotDeclared" } },

  receipts: [
    "**a unit variant's phantom ZST marker is emitted beside a type definition of the same name** (INVALID STATE: v1.compiler.emit_rust collect_phantom_zst_markers emits `pub struct X;` for a closure-unique unit variant X, skipping names a shadow predicate found declared in the module. That predicate recognized type aliases and opaque declarations but not type DEFINITIONS.",

    "HARM: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model declares the records `type AcceptanceNodeReopensActiveFrontier {}` and `type AcceptanceNodeRemainsSuperseded {}` beside the coproduct AcceptanceRevocationDisposition whose arms carry those names, so each record was emitted twice (rustc E0428 and E0119 on every derive, on the rfm-rung-census route; class 1 of stern-bat-401's emitter-debt list).",

    "ROOT CAUSE (DESIGN section 6b): the boundary was the marker decision itself, which answered a question of identity (does this arm denote a declaration?) by comparing spellings over the module's own items, and read the absence of a same-named item as proof that the marker was valid. Module locality does not turn spelling into identity: an arm naming a record the module imports had no same-named local item and was still given a marker (stern-bat-401 side chat, 2026-10-24).",

    "REPAIRED: v1.compiler.emit_rust phantom_marker_decision resolves the arm through resolve_type_decl_reference over EmitGraphInfo.type_decl_items, the identity-keyed index the record-literal phantom decision reads. An arm resolving to a declaration owes no marker. A marker is owed only when the arm resolves to none AND the unit-variant index names this very arm, by declaring span. An ambiguous or kernel-undecided reference, unavailable variant evidence, or evidence naming another node refuses as a located compile_error! item. The spelling predicate phantom_marker_name_shadowed_by_real_type_item is deleted. RED/control: test.claim.phantom_marker_same_named_record_witness same_named_record_suppresses_the_variant_marker and imported_record_arm_owes_no_marker.",

    "RUNG: found at and still mitigatable (the failure is rustc's, and the witnesses are text oracles). Ceiling structurally guaranteed; climbable but unbuilt.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "phantom_marker_decision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.phantom_marker_same_named_record_witness", decl_name: "same_named_record_suppresses_the_variant_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.phantom_marker_same_named_record_witness", decl_name: "imported_record_arm_owes_no_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
